WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.875
♪♪♪

00:00:00.875 --> 00:00:02.877
- [Jeff Johnson:] While a pandemic
swept through our world

00:00:02.877 --> 00:00:05.005
and infected tens of millions—

00:00:05.005 --> 00:00:06.965
- Last night it was the
NBA suspending its season

00:00:06.965 --> 00:00:09.217
after Rudy Gobert of the Utah Jazz

00:00:09.217 --> 00:00:11.386
tested positive for the coronavirus.

00:00:11.386 --> 00:00:14.597
The league will use this hiatus
to determine the next steps

00:00:14.597 --> 00:00:17.183
in dealing with the pandemic.

00:00:17.183 --> 00:00:18.018
- I play for the fans.

00:00:18.018 --> 00:00:19.602
That's what it's all about, so.

00:00:19.602 --> 00:00:21.813
If I show up to an arena and
there ain't no fans in there,

00:00:21.813 --> 00:00:23.565
I ain't playing, so.

00:00:23.565 --> 00:00:25.275
They can do what they wanna do.

00:00:25.275 --> 00:00:27.986
- We all talked shortly after
we shut down the season.

00:00:28.862 --> 00:00:31.656
And of course, we've
always been looking for

00:00:32.991 --> 00:00:35.618
whether or not there is an appropriate

00:00:36.619 --> 00:00:40.832
and safe way in which we
can resume basketball.

00:00:40.832 --> 00:00:42.625
- [Reporter:] Avery Bradley has decided

00:00:42.625 --> 00:00:44.419
not to enter the bubble.

00:00:44.419 --> 00:00:46.713
- [Reporter:] Trevor Ariza
opted out of the bubble.

00:00:46.713 --> 00:00:47.672
- [Reporter:] That I heard.

00:00:47.672 --> 00:00:49.257
- [Reporter:] Mavericks
center Willie Cauley-Stein

00:00:49.257 --> 00:00:52.218
saying he's decided to sit
out the resumed NBA season.

00:00:52.218 --> 00:00:53.344
- [Jeff J.:] Another crisis,

00:00:53.344 --> 00:00:55.305
with roots hundreds of years long

00:00:55.305 --> 00:00:57.348
and tied to our country's history,

00:00:57.348 --> 00:01:00.894
brought Americans to the
streets demanding change.

00:01:00.894 --> 00:01:04.898
Police killing George Floyd
had to mark a turning point.

00:01:04.898 --> 00:01:08.109
- Police shootings and police
killing of African Americans

00:01:08.109 --> 00:01:10.111
like myself, this isn't new.

00:01:10.111 --> 00:01:12.030
It's just everyone has iPhones now,

00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:13.031
so it's getting recorded.

00:01:13.031 --> 00:01:15.241
- [Reporter:] It has been a painful night

00:01:15.241 --> 00:01:18.161
of violence and protests in Minneapolis.

00:01:18.161 --> 00:01:23.166
- It is your duty not to
burn your own house down

00:01:23.291 --> 00:01:25.293
for anger with an enemy.

00:01:25.293 --> 00:01:27.420
- [Reporter:] Breonna
Taylor, a 26-year-old EMT,

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:29.714
was shot eight times by police.

00:01:29.714 --> 00:01:31.049
- [Protester:] Say her name!

00:01:32.008 --> 00:01:34.511
- [Group:] Breonna Taylor!

00:01:34.511 --> 00:01:36.805
- [Jeff J.:] Who was listening
to the Black community?

00:01:36.805 --> 00:01:38.598
- I got brothers, I got
sisters, I got friends

00:01:38.598 --> 00:01:41.101
that are in the streets, that are out here,

00:01:41.101 --> 00:01:42.393
that haven't made it to this level,

00:01:42.393 --> 00:01:43.603
that are experiencing it,

00:01:43.603 --> 00:01:46.147
that are getting pulled
over. Just discrimination

00:01:46.147 --> 00:01:46.981
day after day.

00:01:46.981 --> 00:01:49.734
Dealing with the same, the same bullshit,

00:01:49.734 --> 00:01:51.778
and this is systematic.

00:01:51.778 --> 00:01:53.655
- [Jeff J.:] While the
coronavirus reared its head,

00:01:53.655 --> 00:01:56.199
so did the realities of systemic racism.

00:01:56.199 --> 00:01:58.076
- [Group:] George Floyd!

00:01:58.076 --> 00:02:00.078
- [Jeff J.:] Long felt by
Black people in America

00:02:00.078 --> 00:02:03.248
and too long ignored by so many others.

00:02:03.248 --> 00:02:05.583
- To see all you guys come together

00:02:05.583 --> 00:02:07.460
for one cause, for justice, for peace,

00:02:09.504 --> 00:02:12.298
I'm just happy, man, and
I’ll try to join you guys,

00:02:12.298 --> 00:02:15.009
but continue to stick together.

00:02:15.009 --> 00:02:15.844
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
60
00:02:15,872 --&gt; 00:02:16,705
- [Protester:] What do we want?

00:02:16.678 --> 00:02:17.512
- [Group:] Justice!

00:02:17.512 --> 00:02:18.346
- [Protester:] When do we want it?

00:02:18.346 --> 00:02:19.848
- [Group:] Now!

00:02:19.848 --> 00:02:20.890
- [Protester:] What do we want?

00:02:20.890 --> 00:02:21.724
- [Group:] Justice!

00:02:21.724 --> 00:02:22.684
- [Protester:] When do we want it?

00:02:22.684 --> 00:02:23.685
- [Group:] Now!

00:02:23.685 --> 00:02:25.311
- We need to take the time to go home

00:02:25.311 --> 00:02:28.523
and figure out every single
person who represents us

00:02:28.523 --> 00:02:30.108
and decide if they're
part of the problem

00:02:30.108 --> 00:02:31.734
or part of the solution.

00:02:31.734 --> 00:02:34.195
- [Jeff J.:] Meanwhile,
basketball moved into a bubble.

00:02:34.195 --> 00:02:36.156
- Getting ready to take off to Orlando.

00:02:36.156 --> 00:02:38.324
Check into this bubble.

00:02:38.324 --> 00:02:40.410
- [Jeff J.:] Would this
bubble be a success?

00:02:40.410 --> 00:02:42.871
♪♪♪

00:02:42.871 --> 00:02:44.998
The country asked for
sports to bring healing.

00:02:44.998 --> 00:02:48.334
- I chose Black Lives Matter
because Black lives matter.

00:02:48.334 --> 00:02:50.461
- [Jeff J.:] Black Lives Matter on buses,

00:02:50.461 --> 00:02:52.714
on the court, on jerseys.

00:02:52.714 --> 00:02:54.632
- A lot of people
kinda use this analogy,

00:02:54.632 --> 00:02:56.843
talking about Black Lives
Matter is a movement.

00:02:56.843 --> 00:02:58.178
It's not a movement.

00:02:58.178 --> 00:03:00.305
When you Black, it's not a movement.

00:03:00.305 --> 00:03:01.181
It's a lifestyle.

00:03:01.181 --> 00:03:03.016
- [Jeff J.:] The league
promised to say their names,

00:03:03.016 --> 00:03:04.976
to say her name.

00:03:04.976 --> 00:03:06.519
Justice for Breonna.

00:03:06.519 --> 00:03:07.729
- I want her family to know,

00:03:07.729 --> 00:03:10.106
and I want the state of Kentucky to know,

00:03:10.106 --> 00:03:13.109
that we feel for it and we want justice.

00:03:13.109 --> 00:03:15.612
- I have pretty much every possible name

00:03:15.612 --> 00:03:17.280
of someone that's died
from police brutality

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:18.198
or police violence,

00:03:18.198 --> 00:03:19.949
and on the back too.

00:03:21.576 --> 00:03:23.453
- [Jeff J.:] But the
change that is necessary,

00:03:23.453 --> 00:03:25.914
many wondered if its
momentum would be lost

00:03:25.914 --> 00:03:27.582
inside the walls of a new arena.

00:03:29.209 --> 00:03:32.212
When players said there
was not enough changing,

00:03:32.212 --> 00:03:33.546
basketball stopped.

00:03:33.546 --> 00:03:36.633
[Buzzer]

00:03:36.633 --> 00:03:37.550
- Breaking news now:

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:40.637
NBA television has just announced
that the Milwaukee Bucks

00:03:40.637 --> 00:03:43.890
are boycotting the NBA playoff game

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:45.934
that is scheduled to happen right now.

00:03:45.934 --> 00:03:47.936
- Our focus today cannot be on basketball.

00:03:47.936 --> 00:03:50.313
- We are calling for
justice for Jacob Blake

00:03:50.313 --> 00:03:52.690
and demand the officers
be held accountable.

00:03:53.524 --> 00:03:56.319
- You know, you watch a guy get shot

00:03:56.319 --> 00:03:58.821
in front of his entire family,

00:03:58.821 --> 00:04:01.824
and then right underneath
that video is somebody saying,

00:04:01.824 --> 00:04:03.785
"Hey, well, he should've
just listened to the police."

00:04:03.785 --> 00:04:07.497
So, like, you take all that in,
whether you register it or not,

00:04:07.497 --> 00:04:10.124
whether you realize what
you're looking at or not,

00:04:10.124 --> 00:04:13.044
you're taking that in, and
that depreciation of life,

00:04:13.044 --> 00:04:17.340
and, you know, kinda the—you get numb
to what you're looking at,

00:04:17.340 --> 00:04:19.634
and you almost start to question yourself.

00:04:19.634 --> 00:04:22.428
- As a Black man, as a former player,

00:04:22.428 --> 00:04:25.640
I think it's best for me
to support the players

00:04:25.640 --> 00:04:27.892
and just not be here tonight.

00:04:27.892 --> 00:04:29.727
- [Jeff J.:] They demanded change.

00:04:29.727 --> 00:04:32.855
- We're not trying to defund the police

00:04:32.855 --> 00:04:34.607
and take all their money away.

00:04:34.607 --> 00:04:36.985
We're trying to get them to protect us,

00:04:38.486 --> 00:04:40.446
just like they protect everybody else.

00:04:40.446 --> 00:04:42.865
- The job isn't done yet.

00:04:42.865 --> 00:04:45.994
And we can't stop until
Black lives really do matter.

00:04:45.994 --> 00:04:47.537
- [Jeff J.:] They sought justice.

00:04:47.537 --> 00:04:49.122
They urged us to vote.

00:04:49.122 --> 00:04:52.125
- Hopefully, the initiatives
that we came together,

00:04:52.125 --> 00:04:55.461
that we partnered with, voting and sites

00:04:55.461 --> 00:04:56.754
and arenas and things of that nature,

00:04:56.754 --> 00:04:59.924
hopefully years on down the line,

00:04:59.924 --> 00:05:02.969
America is in a better place,

00:05:02.969 --> 00:05:04.721
that you can look back to
this moment and be like,

00:05:04.721 --> 00:05:08.683
"That was one of the catapults
that kinda got it going."

00:05:08.683 --> 00:05:10.351
- I'm proud to announce that we have

00:05:10.351 --> 00:05:13.021
over 90 percent of our league registered to vote.

00:05:13.021 --> 00:05:15.356
Fifteen teams are 100 percent registered.

00:05:15.356 --> 00:05:18.109
And the job that guys have been doing

00:05:18.109 --> 00:05:21.696
just to be a little bit more
educated on the situations

00:05:21.696 --> 00:05:24.407
and getting people out,
recruiting poll workers

00:05:24.407 --> 00:05:26.284
and things like that,

00:05:26.284 --> 00:05:29.037
the bubble has been an
unbelievable blessing.

00:05:29.037 --> 00:05:31.914
Our players are continuing to do the work,

00:05:31.914 --> 00:05:34.459
and we're grateful, and
we're gonna keep working.

00:05:34.459 --> 00:05:37.045
- [Jeff J.:] Can we call
this bubble a success?

00:05:37.045 --> 00:05:38.379
- I think the biggest thing

00:05:38.379 --> 00:05:40.298
was us being able to
come together as a group

00:05:40.298 --> 00:05:43.259
and try to figure out ways to
continue to impact society.

00:05:43.259 --> 00:05:44.510
I think we’ve continued to do that,

00:05:44.510 --> 00:05:46.637
and hopefully we continue to uplift

00:05:46.637 --> 00:05:48.431
and put light on some of the injustices

00:05:48.431 --> 00:05:49.932
that we're seeing in America.

00:05:49.932 --> 00:05:52.060
- We came down here for a reason,

00:05:52.060 --> 00:05:53.811
and obviously to win a championship,

00:05:53.811 --> 00:05:55.396
but to spread the message.

00:05:55.396 --> 00:05:57.440
We stopped playing and continued playing

00:05:57.440 --> 00:05:59.067
because we're gonna continue
to preach our message,

00:05:59.067 --> 00:05:59.942
not just for the game.

00:05:59.942 --> 00:06:03.571
But I'm very happy with
the way things went

00:06:03.571 --> 00:06:05.740
as far as being able to
come back on the floor

00:06:05.740 --> 00:06:06.949
and the NBA and the owners

00:06:06.949 --> 00:06:08.659
and us agreeing on certain things.

00:06:08.659 --> 00:06:10.495
And I hope this,

00:06:10.495 --> 00:06:13.247
as these playoffs go,
as everybody watches,

00:06:13.247 --> 00:06:16.000
we continue to push what's
really needed in this world.

00:06:18.211 --> 00:06:19.462
- It was challenging.

00:06:19.462 --> 00:06:22.215
It was well put-together.

00:06:23.216 --> 00:06:25.218
The NBA and the teams and the players

00:06:25.218 --> 00:06:27.136
did a hell of a job sacrificing.

00:06:27.136 --> 00:06:30.681
We used our platform for
our voices to be heard

00:06:30.681 --> 00:06:32.683
in the social injustices.

00:06:32.683 --> 00:06:35.061
Getting guys to go out there to vote.

00:06:35.061 --> 00:06:36.437
Justice for Breonna Taylor.

00:06:37.522 --> 00:06:39.023
Justice for everybody,

00:06:39.023 --> 00:06:40.650
every Black American out there

00:06:40.650 --> 00:06:45.113
that are being harmed by
police and police brutality.

00:06:45.113 --> 00:06:47.281
- [Jeff J.:] There are still questions,

00:06:47.281 --> 00:06:48.366
but we are listening.

00:06:49.200 --> 00:06:52.161
- My skin color should not
determine whether I live or die.

00:06:53.079 --> 00:06:55.998
This is a human civil right
crisis that's going on.

00:06:55.998 --> 00:06:56.833
- The game was great.

00:06:56.833 --> 00:06:57.667
We won by two.

00:06:57.667 --> 00:06:58.709
But at the end of the day,

00:06:58.709 --> 00:07:00.253
Breonna Taylor's killers are still free.

00:07:00.253 --> 00:07:01.087
There are so many different things

00:07:01.087 --> 00:07:02.046
that we can honestly talk about.

00:07:02.046 --> 00:07:04.090
I'm gonna continue to
talk about Breonna Taylor

00:07:04.090 --> 00:07:05.800
cuz that's near and dear to me.

00:07:05.800 --> 00:07:08.386
- One thing for me is that
Breonna Taylor’s killers

00:07:08.386 --> 00:07:10.888
still are roaming around free.

00:07:10.888 --> 00:07:12.974
So I think I just wanna focus on that

00:07:12.974 --> 00:07:15.518
with these interviews
and things like that.

00:07:15.518 --> 00:07:16.811
So I just wanna keep the focus there.

00:07:16.811 --> 00:07:20.231
- We wanna make sure that Daniel Cameron

00:07:20.231 --> 00:07:22.942
will arrest the cops and the officers involved

00:07:22.942 --> 00:07:25.778
with Breonna Taylor's death.

00:07:25.778 --> 00:07:28.990
- My answer is gonna be
justice for Breonna Taylor.

00:07:28.990 --> 00:07:30.741
That's gonna be my answer for everything.

00:07:30.741 --> 00:07:33.703
So I'm just letting
you guys know that now.

00:07:33.703 --> 00:07:36.831
- [Tobias Harris:] That's gonna be
my answer for every question.

00:07:36.831 --> 00:07:37.874
- [Interviewer:] Fair enough.

00:07:37.874 --> 00:07:41.752
- For Daniel Cameron to step
up and to do what's right,

00:07:41.752 --> 00:07:44.088
and that's the only
message I got today.

00:07:44.088 --> 00:07:45.673
I appreciate everybody. Thanks.

00:07:46.632 --> 00:07:47.842
- [Interviewer:] Thanks, T.

00:07:47.842 --> 00:07:48.843
- [LeBron James:] Where do we go from here?

00:07:48.843 --> 00:07:50.595
We don't stop.

00:07:50.595 --> 00:07:52.305
Obviously when the season ends

00:07:54.098 --> 00:07:56.517
in less than a week,

00:07:57.602 --> 00:07:59.645
that everyone disperses and goes back,

00:07:59.645 --> 00:08:02.940
but I hope that people
continue to use their platform,

00:08:02.940 --> 00:08:05.735
use their individual
social media platforms

00:08:05.735 --> 00:08:08.321
if they're doing it that way,

00:08:08.321 --> 00:08:12.700
if you're an individual that
goes into your community

00:08:12.700 --> 00:08:14.327
and does it that way,

00:08:15.411 --> 00:08:18.706
however that you can continue to create change

00:08:19.624 --> 00:08:21.042
for the better of all of us.

00:08:22.293 --> 00:08:25.838
I think it only makes us all better.

00:08:25.838 --> 00:08:28.508
- [Protester:] Say her name!

00:08:28.508 --> 00:08:30.593
- [Group:] Breonna Taylor!

